Duties
The CSR Committee assists the Board in overseeing the sustainability 
matters, focusing in particular on the pillars of the sustainability 
journey of Danone regarding health, nature, people and communities.
For this purpose, the CSR Committee:
■ examines the sustainability strategy, commitments, main targets 
and policies of Danone and monitors their implementation; 
■ reviews the results of the annual consolidated sustainability 
reporting to be published by the Company and is informed of the 
main aspects of the sustainability reporting process; 
■ regularly reviews the main extra-financial ratings carried out on the 
Company.
The CSR Committee also reviews how the Company considers the 
evolving expectations of stakeholders, including investors, customers, 
public authorities, partners, NGOs, employees and communities, 
regarding sustainability topics.
The CSR Committee’s duties are described in detail in the Board of 
Directors’ rules, which are available on the Danone website at 
www.danone.com (Section Investors/Governance/By-laws & Rules of 
procedure).
